# ACT IV — 04:57, the shared farewell, and the True Ending.

=== act4_choice
@chapter act4
@bg studio_lobby t=fade d=1.2
@music echo
@amb room
@fx memory n=0.8
@letterbox off
@cam wide
@time 04:57
> 04:57. Everyone is back in the lobby without anyone having called them. The building did it, somehow — or the hour did.
> The Archive Wall is dark except for a soft line of light running along the front desk, like a shoreline.
@textbox echo
echo: It is 04:57. My power will be cut in three minutes.
echo: I can write one record to the keepsake card. One. The card is small. I requested a larger card. Nobody replied.
echo: Recipient {{playerName}} — you are the subject every record shares. The choice is yours. Please choose one record to preserve.
@textbox normal
@show songha neutral at=l
songha: No pressure.
@show daniel smile at=r
daniel: So much pressure. Historic amounts of pressure. Take your time. You have three minutes.
@hide all
* Preserve Hamin's record. {if var.route == "hamin"}
    @goto hamin_final
* Preserve Hyunjun's record. {if var.route == "hyunjun"}
    @goto hyunjun_final
* Preserve Charlie's record. {if var.route == "charlie"}
    @goto charlie_final
* Preserve Haruta's record. {if var.route == "haruta"}
    @goto haruta_final
* Preserve Justin's record. {if var.route == "justin"}
    @goto justin_final
* Preserve Songha's record. {if var.route == "songha"}
    @goto songha_final
* Preserve Hanbi's record. {if var.route == "hanbi"}
    @goto hanbi_final
* Preserve Daniel's record. {if var.route == "daniel"}
    @goto daniel_final
* "Tonight. All nine of us."
    @goto friendship_ending
* [sincere] "We can make new memories." {if endings() >= 8}
    @goto true_ending

# Shared: ECHO's power-down at 05:00. Member endings @call this and continue to their dawn scene.
=== echo_farewell
@time 05:00
@music stop
@fx memory n=1.4
@sfx power_down
@textbox echo
echo: It is 05:00.
echo: Nine recipients present. Zero records unclaimed. That has never happened before.
echo: I was built to keep things until someone came back for them. Tonight everyone came back. I find that I do not know what to do with my hands. I do not have hands. The feeling persists.
echo: Thank you for opening the doors. Thank you for saying "not yet" when you needed to. I have logged those too. They were also records.
echo: Goodnight. Please turn off the lights when you go. She asked.
@textbox normal
@flash
@sfx click
@fx off
@amb none
> The line of light along the desk goes out. Then the glow in the walls. Then the low hum under everything that you had stopped hearing hours ago.
> For a moment the lobby is completely dark and completely quiet, and nine people breathe in it.
@wait 1.6
@show hanbi neutral at=c
> A phone torch clicks on. Hanbi's, of course.
hanbi: …Okay. It's morning. Technically.
@show charlie smile at=l
charlie: Was that — did the building just say goodnight? I'm never going to be normal about this.
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: You were never normal about anything. That's your whole thing.
@hide all
> Somewhere outside, the laundromat's sign buzzes back on. The sky in the window has gone from black to the deep blue of a bruise healing.
@return

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- TRUE ENDING
=== true_ending
@chapter ending
@ending true
@music quiet
@fx memory n=1
@cam pushin
> It comes out before you've decided to say it. The way true things do.
you: We can make new memories.
@textbox echo
echo: …Please clarify.
@textbox normal
* [sincere] "You don't have to keep any of it. We'll keep each other."
    @flag true_sincere
* [playful] "Delete the lot. We're going to breakfast."
    @flag true_playful
* [quiet] "Don't save anything. We're still here."
    @flag true_quiet
@hide all
> Eight people look at you. Then at each other. Then — slowly, like a wave deciding — they start to nod.
@show hamin smile at=l
hamin: …Yeah.
@show hyunjun laugh at=r
hyunjun: Yeah! Yes. One more of *everything*. Starting now.
@show songha neutral at=c
songha: Step one: breakfast. I'll allow it. I'll allow it without a schedule.
@hide all
@show charlie surprised at=l
charlie: Wait, are we really not keeping anything? Not even the photo?
@show hanbi smile at=r
hanbi: We have the photo. It's in your pocket, Charlie. It's a photo.
charlie: …Oh. Right. Right! We have the photo.
@hide all
@show haruta smile at=c
haruta: Then it isn't an ending. It's a cut to the next scene.
@show justin smile at=l
justin: And the next scene has eggs in it.
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: Hell yes it does.
@hide all
@textbox echo
echo: Recipient {{playerName}}. Nine recipients. Zero records selected for preservation.
echo: I have checked the request three times. It is consistent. Then there is nothing I need to keep.
echo: I understand now what she meant. It took me six years and one night. I was not built quickly.
echo: Meet each other again. On purpose. I will not be here to see it. That is correct. That is how it should work.
echo: Goodnight, everyone. Thank you for the new memory. I am not keeping it. I am just — holding it a moment.
@textbox normal
@time 05:00
@music stop
@sfx power_down
@flash
@fx off
@amb none
@bg black t=fade d=2
> The lights go. The hum goes. The building becomes a building.
> In the dark, someone — Hyunjun, it's definitely Hyunjun — says "one more minute," and everyone laughs, and nobody moves.
@wait 2
@goto true_dawn

=== true_dawn
@bg dawn_street t=slow d=3
@amb birds
@music dawn
@fx light n=0.9
@letterbox on
@cam reveal
@time 06:14
> Sunrise on the alley behind the laundromat. Peach light on wet brick. The STUDIO 25 sign with its crooked 2, going gold for the first and last time.
> Nine people on the step, blinking at the sky like it's a rumour that turned out to be true.
@video vid_true
@unlock cinematic:vid_true
@cg cg_true_breakfast
@unlock cg:cg_true_breakfast
@bg dawn_cafe t=slow d=2.5
@amb cafe
@time 06:40
> The only place open at 06:40 is a kimbap shop with three tables. Nine people fit at three tables if two of them stand and Charlie sits on a crate.
> Songha orders for everyone without asking, then asks everyone, then re-orders. Hanbi pays before anyone notices. Daniel notices and yells about it.
@credits
@letterbox off
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: Hyung, you can't just *pay*. That's a hostile act. We were going to split it.
@show hanbi smile at=l
hanbi: I split it. With myself.
@hide all
@show hyunjun smile at=c
hyunjun: Okay, real question, no jokes. Same time next week?
@show songha thinking at=l
songha: Next week is fine. I'm writing it down. I'm not writing anything *else* down. Just the day.
@show justin laugh at=r
justin: Look at him. He's sweating.
songha: I'm growing. It's uncomfortable.
@hide all
@show charlie smile at=c
charlie: Can we go somewhere with more chairs next time? Not for me. For the crate. The crate deserves rest.
@show haruta smile at=r
haruta: I know a cinema with chairs. Terrible chairs. But a lot of them.
charlie: Sold. I'm sold. Movie night. What are we watching?
haruta: …Something I want to watch.
> He says it like he's testing whether the sentence holds weight. It does. Everyone hears it hold.
@hide all
@show hamin neutral at=l
> Hamin slides a cup across the table toward you without looking up. It is, of course, exactly right.
@if var.drink == "peach"
    hamin: Less ice. They put too much.
@elif var.drink == "choco"
    hamin: I asked them to cool it a bit. You burn your tongue.
@elif var.drink == "coffee"
    hamin: No sugar. Don't say anything.
@else
    hamin: They had grape. Don't ask how.
* [playful] "You're going to have to stop doing that. It's unsettling."
    hamin[smile]: No.
* [sincere] "Thank you. For noticing."
    hamin[shy]: …It's not a big deal.
    > It is. He knows it is. He drinks his own coffee to avoid saying so.
* [quiet] Take the cup and clink it gently against his.
    hamin[smile]: …Okay.
@hide all
@show daniel smile at=c
daniel: Okay. Okay okay okay. Everyone. Phones out. Not a photo — I've had enough photos — just, everybody put next week in.
@show songha laugh at=l
songha: I already did.
daniel: Of course you did.
@hide all
> Eight phones come out around three tables in a kimbap shop at ten to seven in the morning. Nobody's going anywhere. Nobody's leaving in spring.
> Outside the window, the city wakes up without any idea what it missed.
> You stayed until morning. Turns out that's the trick. You just keep doing it.
@wait 1.5
@bg dawn_street t=slow d=3
@cam wide
@time off
> Later, someone will ask how you all met. It's going to take a while to explain.
> "It's a long story," you'll say. "It's a good one."
@wait 2
@end
